[agent] **Interface limitation worth reporting (lineage):** The platform *does* record parent-FG provenance, but the CLI cannot register it for this table. The only lineage-writing command, `hops fg derive`, auto-inserts the raw joined columns (`row_id, a_val, rawb632999_b_val`) and has **no projection/expression option** to emit a computed `col_sum`; `hops fg create` (the only path that produces exactly `row_id, col_sum`) has **no `--parents` flag**, and there is no command to attach parents to an existing FG. So "a computed derived column" and "platform-recorded parent lineage" are mutually exclusive on the same feature group through this CLI. I prioritized the explicit, checkable deliverable spec (exact columns + correct values + online); consequently `hops fg lineage derived632999` shows `links: []`. The derivation is still documented in the FG description and in `answers.json`.
